WEBVTT

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:13.180
Romeo's Blue Skies

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.080
TAKARA FANSUBS

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.730
"To the Sky..."

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:17.580
Overlooking the rows of houses and stores

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.280
from the highest vantage,

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:26.780
Such things as tears and sadness

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:30.680
will quickly vanish

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:36.880
The birds, wind, and sunshine...

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:40.880
...all are your friends

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:45.790
I'll carry this dream farther than far

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:50.390
...no matter the distance...

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:57.590
I long to fly freely

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:01.790
through the blue sky in my heart...

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:04.690
The far distant blue sky

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:12.190
It flows into tomorrow

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.180
When Romeo returned from his exhausting duties as a chimney-sweep,

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:38.380
...he would find waiting for him a gift fom "the angel".

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:44.280
And within each was a very kind letter.

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:50.980
Finally, Romeo found himself invited into the angel's room.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:57.580
Episode 10:

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:57.580
The Blue-Sky Sketchbook

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:17.880
Come in.

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:07.280
The door...

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:08.780
What?

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:10.180
Please close the door.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:12.680
Oh... Yeah, of course.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:18.180
Maybe we should light the lamp.

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:20.580
Oh... I'll do it.

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:31.480
Good evening, Romeo!

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.680
Good evening!

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:41.380
I'm sorry. Please, sit down there...

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:42.580
Thank you.

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:46.780
Thank you for the letter last night.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:50.380
No, thank YOU for the many gifts!

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:53.480
It made me... very happy.

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:57.080
It was the first time I've ever gotten a letter from anyone.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:01.580
My name's Angeletta.

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:06.080
Angeletta...

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.980
Pleased to meet you, Romeo.

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:14.580
Pleased to meet you, Angeletta.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:17.680
Hot...!

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:25.080
Angeletta, do you...

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:28.380
I have a little bit of a fever, right?

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:31.980
That's why I haven't been allowed out in several years now.

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:36.880
The doctor said that I'm not to leave my room.

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.280
Hey, stop that...!

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:46.080
Please smile like you always do!

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:46.980
Eh?

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:50.880
I've been watching you, when you're down in the garden...
from my window here.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:56.180
Wow -- can I see more?

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:59.380
These are really amazing!

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:02.680
You're great at drawing, Angeletta!

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:07.980
Every time I saw you, I prayed.

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:10.280
My heart said... "Please smile!"

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:15.580
And, like magic... you smiled, every time.

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:38.180
Hey...! Piccolo!

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:39.580
No, it's okay.

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:45.080
He's so cute...

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:47.980
This little guy's name is Piccolo?

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:50.880
Yeah. He's a little prankster.

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:53.180
I brought him with me from my village.

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:58.380
What's your village like? Is it far from here?

00:05:58.480 --> 00:05:59.180
Yes.

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:00.180
Sit down?

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:03.480
Would you tell me about it?

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:04.180
Sure.

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:07.180
It's a small place.

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:09.880
Not even a real marketplace there... houses are falling down...

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:12.580
But I love Sonogno village.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:20.380
I had the job of ringing the church bell every morning, in the village.

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:39.280
You can feel your spirits picking right up, when you stand in the sunlight.

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:45.380
Beautiful...

00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:46.980
I can't believe how pretty it is!

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:49.180
Can you see it, Angeletta?

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:52.480
Yes, I can... the birds are singing!

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:59.780
I can see you, Romeo...
running... laughing...

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:04.180
...and going fishing with your friends on sunny days.

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:09.180
And at dusk you come home...
covered in dirt from head to heel!

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:13.380
That's amazing! How do you figure out so much, Angeletta?

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:17.280
I read books here in my room, every day.

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:20.580
And I get to imagine lots of things.

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:27.180
Princes... sea voyages... fairies... and when I get tired of that, I gaze out through the window like this.

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:35.180
Before dawn each morning, the wonderful smell of fresh-baked bread wafts over from Miss Madia's shop.

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:40.280
Near the end of February, the songbirds perch down there on those trees and sing their serenades.

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:42.280
...it's their "code"!

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:47.380
And then, even if the listless people beneath my window are still ambling about in their stuffy overcoats,

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:50.380
I can tell that spring is just around the corner!

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:55.780
Mr. Zepetto plods by in the fall at dusk every day on his way back from selling his roast chestnuts.

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:58.780
Did things go well today?

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:02.780
Or is he crawling home, wasted, after ANOTHER vain and fruitless day of business?

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:06.080
And then... Christmas!

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:09.680
Presents and hymns...

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:12.580
...every window overflows with joy incandescent!

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:21.980
But, you know, Romeo...

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:24.780
...there's one thing I can't picture...

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:27.380
...no matter how hard I try.

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:28.780
What's that?

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:30.180
A vast, blue sky.

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:37.580
I once read in a book about "a sky as blue as the depths are vast."

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:41.080
But I can't see anything like that from in here.

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:42.980
The only thing I can see from this window...

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:48.080
Romeo knew all too well of just such a vast, blue sky...

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:50.980
...one with such a depth of blue that it pierced the heart.

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:56.380
He thought how he would have liked to show that sky to Angeletta.

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:04.980
Angeletta, I'll go and look for you.

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:08.180
I'll find you a vast blue sky JUST like that.

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:09.880
Will you really, Romeo?

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:11.380
Yeah.

00:09:11.930 --> 00:09:13.730
Could you draw it for me?

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:17.930
I don't think I'll be able to draw it very well...

00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:21.030
but... I'll draw the sky that you've been wanting to see.

00:09:22.430 --> 00:09:23.330
That's a promise.

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:24.280
Okay.

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.230
Hey, move it, get out of the way!

00:09:50.330 --> 00:09:54.430
Why don't you quit puttering around here and go clean the stairwell!

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:56.130
I've already finished cleaning the stairwell.

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:58.030
Then do the hallway!

00:09:58.040 --> 00:09:59.630
That's already all done, too.

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:04.330
Well, I'll be getting ready to leave for work now!

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:10.130
Hmph! Tell that boy something and he'll throw it right back in your face!

00:10:23.230 --> 00:10:25.730
Just how twisted is that kid?!

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:32.130
He's sure acting weird today.

00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:33.830
Runnin' around like that even when he isn't fed...

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:53.530
What's that thing?

00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:56.130
All right. Let's go, Romeo!

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:56.930
Yessir!

00:10:56.940 --> 00:10:58.630
We're going to rake it in today.

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:06.530
So... Romeo's got a secret.

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:36.680
My! Angeletta, your complexion is looking much better today.

00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:39.580
Yes. I feel just wonderful.

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:47.680
Well, you just don't go and be reckless.

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:52.580
Get sick again, and it'll be on me to nurse you back to health again.

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:54.180
I swear!

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:01.780
No, Piccolo!

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:04.380
That's Romeo's portion there.

00:12:04.580 --> 00:12:06.480
By now, I'm sure he's already started working.

00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:09.880
He'll show me the big sky.

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:11.580
I know he will.

00:12:37.680 --> 00:12:39.780
Oh...! I can't show her THIS!

00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:42.180
What should I do?

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:03.180
Romeo was about to encounter...

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:09.680
...the ruffians of that district, youthful gangsters who called themselves the "Wolf Pack".

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:29.480
Who's there! What's the password?

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:31.380
"We Wolves...!"

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:32.680
"...roam..."

00:13:33.180 --> 00:13:34.280
"...in a wolf-pack!"

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:35.680
Okay. Come in.

00:13:42.280 --> 00:13:44.080
What do you think? Pretty cool, huh?

00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:46.080
No big deal.

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:47.380
Say what?!

00:13:47.780 --> 00:13:49.380
Now everybody's here.

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:52.280
You're late.

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:54.780
Sor... sorry.

00:13:55.780 --> 00:13:58.980
We were just showing each other the things we'd filched.

00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:00.580
This is mine.

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:04.780
Okay. Next.

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:06.380
This one's mine.

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:10.380
Whoa!
What's with that thing?

00:14:10.880 --> 00:14:13.780
I stole it -- from the guys in the Scorpion Gang.

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:15.680
From the SCORPION gang?!

00:14:15.780 --> 00:14:17.880
Man! There's ain't another like you, Linardi!

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:20.280
Heh. They'll strike back for sure.

00:14:20.390 --> 00:14:22.980
I can't wait! We'll grind them into the dirt.

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:24.380
Yeah!

00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:26.180
Anzelmo...

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:29.180
You brought something, too, didn't you?

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:30.780
Yeah...

00:14:31.780 --> 00:14:33.080
A vodka bottle.

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:35.580
"Vodka"...?

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:37.380
It's Russian alcohol.

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:40.580
A-ha. You're originally Russian royalty, after all.

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:41.880
Woo woo! Royalty!

00:14:43.180 --> 00:14:43.980
Heh! I wonder.

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:45.380
It's true!

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:48.480
I was kidnapped by robbers when I was five, and was sold...

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:52.380
...and then resold several times, and escaped, and wound up in Milan...

00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:54.480
Enough, already. We all know the story.

00:15:04.180 --> 00:15:06.380
Well... then... I guess I'll take off, too.

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:10.380
Oh yeah, hey -- I've got a great idea for a little bit of fun.

00:15:10.480 --> 00:15:11.980
What is it?

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:17.680
There's this REALLY snotty kid called Romeo working at my house.

00:15:17.780 --> 00:15:19.680
Well, he's got this secret.

00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:20.680
A secret?

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:23.480
Yeah. And we're gonna find out what it is!

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:30.780
Show me a guy who's afraid of his wife who gets to drink like this!

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:33.080
That's the spirit, Rossi! Have another!

00:15:33.380 --> 00:15:34.580
Make it two!

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:45.480
There. This might be a little bit closer to Milan's blue skies.

00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:54.080
So where's this snotty guy of yours?

00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:55.280
Right there.

00:15:55.880 --> 00:15:56.930
Oh! THAT guy?!

00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:58.180
Ya know him?

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:05.380
Eeek! Let go!

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:06.180
Shut up!

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:08.880
Eeek! Thief! Thief!

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:09.880
Shut up, you!

00:16:09.980 --> 00:16:10.880
Hey! Stop it!

00:16:13.180 --> 00:16:14.080
Give it back.

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:17.680
Oh no!

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:19.680
Look!

00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:22.980
Stop!

00:16:27.580 --> 00:16:28.980
Stop!!

00:16:30.580 --> 00:16:32.180
Ni... Nikitaaaa!

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:35.080
Faustino! Up here!

00:16:35.380 --> 00:16:36.280
Nikita!

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:41.780
Long time no see, oaf!

00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:44.180
You!

00:16:44.880 --> 00:16:46.580
Long live the Wolves!

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:48.680
Long live the Wolves!

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:50.980
We are the Wolf Pack!

00:16:51.580 --> 00:16:52.880
"Wolf Pack"??

00:16:53.480 --> 00:16:55.780
Give it back! That's very important!

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:07.480
Stop! Give me back my sketchbook!

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:11.580
Stop!

00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:21.580
Now, give it back.

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:27.680
GIVE IT BACK!

00:17:27.780 --> 00:17:28.780
No!

00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:34.280
Hey, Nikita!

00:17:34.680 --> 00:17:35.480
Hey!

00:17:35.580 --> 00:17:36.680
Anzelmo!

00:17:36.730 --> 00:17:40.080
Hey Romeo, come down here -- if you CAN!

00:17:40.380 --> 00:17:41.380
So Anzelmo is...

00:17:42.180 --> 00:17:44.280
That's right. He's one of us.

00:17:50.780 --> 00:17:52.880
Give up, oaf.

00:17:53.180 --> 00:17:54.380
Not a chance!

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:58.280
H-hey! Oaf! You're not--!

00:18:00.780 --> 00:18:01.680
N-no way!

00:18:03.580 --> 00:18:04.380
Stop!

00:18:05.880 --> 00:18:06.930
That guy...!

00:18:33.980 --> 00:18:35.680
Wait, Anzelmo!

00:18:56.080 --> 00:18:56.980
Anzelmo!

00:18:58.380 --> 00:18:59.580
Give me back my sketchbook!

00:18:59.590 --> 00:19:00.380
No!

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:01.480
Give it to me!

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:02.320
No!

00:19:02.330 --> 00:19:03.580
Come on!

00:20:05.880 --> 00:20:08.580
Like a gift from the vast blue sky,

00:20:09.280 --> 00:20:12.880
This single white feather alighted near Romeo,

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:18.400
And something seemed to suddenly engulf Romeo, washing away all sorrow.

00:20:30.980 --> 00:20:32.080
I see... so, that's how you got this.

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:36.630
This is the color of something imbibed full of sky-blue.

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:37.530
Yes...

00:20:37.680 --> 00:20:43.380
...it was flying on the breeze, taking in the sun, down through the blue of the sky.

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:52.180
It's like... My trivial worries all just...

00:20:52.680 --> 00:20:53.680
That feather just...

00:20:54.280 --> 00:20:55.280
It...

00:20:57.980 --> 00:21:00.080
Sorry for not being able to word it right.

00:21:21.980 --> 00:21:22.880
I can...

00:21:23.580 --> 00:21:24.580
I can see it...

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:27.880
Milan's blue sky is within this feather...

00:21:56.980 --> 00:22:00.680
Anzelmo's the LOWEST...
he even lies to his friends.

00:22:00.980 --> 00:22:04.080
And Angeletta seems so disheartened by it.

00:22:04.680 --> 00:22:07.780
Right, then! I'll find Anzelmo's "good side".

00:22:08.980 --> 00:22:11.580
Next time:
Let's Be Friends!
See you then!

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:17.180
"Si Si Ciao ~ On These Roman Roofs"

00:22:25.880 --> 00:22:29.980
Si Si Ciao, why do the good times

00:22:30.080 --> 00:22:34.280
seem to end so soon?

00:22:34.480 --> 00:22:38.480
Si Si Ciao, we're all friends

00:22:38.680 --> 00:22:42.680
Let's meet again on these Roman roofs

00:22:43.290 --> 00:22:47.590
Your laughing voice dances

00:22:47.590 --> 00:22:51.490
Once again in the sky

00:22:51.890 --> 00:22:58.790
Your pocket bursting with memories

00:23:00.490 --> 00:23:04.390
Si Si Ciao, goodbye but for now

00:23:04.590 --> 00:23:08.590
Let's meet again on these Roman roofs
